summary:
  The name rung auditions every row that carries the name again, whatever
  country it is filed under.

history:
  "Rock FM" answered with five exact-name rows from four countries on
  2026-09-21, and on name, domain and bitrate alone the Estonian 320 kb/s
  stream auditioned first for a Spanish listener's dead station, under
  their name and their logo. The ladder now keeps a row only when it sits
  on the station's own domain or in the station's country; a wake-up is
  the one caller that keeps them all. This mutant keeps them all for
  everyone.

target:
  package/contents/ui/HealLogic.js

find:
          if (w.near || anySound === true) keep.push(w); else refused++;

replace:
          if (true) keep.push(w); else refused++;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_heallogic.qml::test_namesakes_from_several_countries_are_not_auditioned.
  Line-neutral.
